Open Robot Arena @VERSION@ — Linux x86_64
Built @DATE@

A native, headless Rust engine for Robot Arena 2: Design & Destroy (Gabriel
Interactive / Infogrames, 2003). It reads the original game's data files
directly: no Windows, no Wine, no emulator.

This package does NOT include the game. Robot Arena 2 is not sold or supported
any more, but it is still its owners' work: you must supply your own copy.
None of its files are copied into this package, the installation, or its
frames.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. What you need

  * Linux x86_64.
  * A working Vulkan driver (Mesa's lavapipe/llvmpipe software driver also
    works). The 2D and 3D renderers are headless wgpu; nothing opens a window.
  * CPython 3.12 with its shared library. See section 3.
  * Your Robot Arena 2 installation. For the shell it needs at least:

        RA2.cfz
        UI/
        Scripts/

    The other tools also use Components/, Arenas/, AI/, Teams/ and the .cfz
    archives, so point them at the complete install.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Unpack and run

    tar xzf ra2-open-robot-arena-@VERSION@-linux-x86_64.tar.gz
    cd ra2-open-robot-arena-@VERSION@-linux-x86_64
    ./run.sh --game "/path/to/Robot Arena 2"

With no options the launcher runs the "botlab" route and writes the frames to

    ~/.local/state/ra2-open-robot-arena/frames

It prints each screen, click and file it writes. Other routes and input
scripts are passed straight to bin/ra2-shell:

    ./run.sh --game "/path/to/Robot Arena 2" --route exhibition
    ./run.sh --game "/path/to/Robot Arena 2" --script my-input.txt --out /tmp/shots

A click script is one command per line: `click x y`, `click "Widget Name"`,
`wait n`, `shot name.png`. The shipped routes are:

    botlab      main menu -> team picker -> team HQ -> robots -> bot lab ->
                chassis tool -> structure step 1      (7 frames)
    exhibition  main menu -> exhibition setup -> arena picker  (3 frames)

The launcher looks for the game in this order: --game, $RA2_GAME_DIR,
$XDG_DATA_HOME/ra2-open-robot-arena/game, game/ beside the launcher (or ../game
when installed), ./local/game upwards from the current directory, then
/usr/local/share/ra2-open-robot-arena/game, /usr/share/ra2-open-robot-arena/game
and /opt/ra2/game. If none is found it prints the three required names and
every path it tried.

The shell is headless: it does not open a window and there is no mouse input.
"Works" below means "renders the original screen data and walks its routes".

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. CPython 3.12 is required (and is not bundled)

ra2-shell, ra2-sim and ra2-duel embed the game's Python through pyo3, and the
binaries are dynamically linked against libpython3.12.so.1.0. The dynamic
loader needs that shared library before main() runs, so `--no-python` does not
remove the dependency. This package does not ship Python; it uses yours.

Check it:

    python3.12 --version
    ldd bin/ra2-shell | grep libpython3.12

Expected: Python 3.12.x, and a line resolving to a real path such as
/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libpython3.12.so.1.0. "not found" means the runtime is
missing. The standard library for 3.12 must be installed too.

Install the runtime (examples; this build is tied to the 3.12 ABI):

    Debian/Ubuntu  sudo apt install python3.12 libpython3.12
    Fedora         sudo dnf install python3.12
    Arch           the rolling python is usually newer than 3.12; install a
                   3.12 build and set both:
                     LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/path/to/3.12/lib
                     PYTHONHOME=/path/to/3.12

The launcher checks the library and the 3.12 standard library before running.
`./run.sh --check-python` prints what it found. A binary built against a
different Python minor version needs a matching runtime; this release is
3.12-only by construction, not by choice of a flag.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Other tools in bin/

  ra2-shell   the shell entry point (boots the main menu, walks routes)
  ra2         data inspector: ra2 info, ra2 obj, ra2 cfz, ra2 arena, ra2 gib,
              ra2 font. Useful for support and for checking an install.
  ra2-render  offscreen renderer: a .gmf part, an assembled .bot robot, or an
              arena .py scene -> PNG.
  ra2-sim     drive one robot around an arena; writes a frame strip.
  ra2-duel    two AI-driven robots fight; writes a frame strip.

Examples (paths are inside your game directory):

    bin/ra2 info "/path/to/Robot Arena 2/Components/mower_blade/mower_blade1.gmf"
    bin/ra2-render "/path/to/Robot Arena 2/AI/Team0/Bot0.bot" scout.png
    bin/ra2-sim "/path/to/Robot Arena 2/Arenas/octagon.py" \
                "/path/to/Robot Arena 2/AI/Team1/Bot0.bot" out/ 6 10
    bin/ra2-duel "/path/to/Robot Arena 2/Arenas/octagon.py" \
                 "/path/to/Robot Arena 2/AI/Team14/Bot2.bot" \
                 "/path/to/Robot Arena 2/AI/Team13/Bot1.bot" out/ 20 12

The 3D tools read the game's own meshes, materials and textures. The script
layer runs the shipped Python 2.2 arenas and AI unmodified on the embedded
interpreter.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. What works, and what does not

Works:
  * Reading all shipped .gmf meshes, .bot robots, .cfz archives, .gib screens,
    .giff fonts, team files and arena scripts.
  * The shell's main menu, team picker, team HQ, robot inventory, bot lab and
    chassis steps, walked by the screens' own notes (headless frames).
  * The exhibition setup and the arena picker, with the 12 arena names.
  * Offscreen rendering of every shipped robot and arena scene.
  * The physics sandbox and two-robot duels, with the shipped Python AI.
  * Booting Scripts/Main.py, the game's own entry point.

Does not work yet:
  * There is no interactive window, mouse or keyboard loop. Frames are PNGs.
  * The actual match (driving, damage, scoring) is the original C++ and is not
    playable through the shell; it stops at the arena picker. ra2-sim and
    ra2-duel are the playable physics paths, headless.
  * Audio, music and video playback are not implemented.
  * The Microsoft/in-game codecs, installers and D3D wrappers in the original
    install (D3D8.dll, dgVoodoo, .exe) are not used.
  * Some fidelity caveats remain (a quarter of stock robots cannot find wheel
    traction, BurstMotor rest poses are approximate, per-part damage is
    calibrated). README.md and docs/06-deferred-fidelity.md in the source tree
    name each one.
  * No game data, mod support, network play or update check.

An honest summary: this is an engine and a verification harness, not a
finished game client. It renders the original data and simulates the original
physics; it does not yet give you the original's window.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. Desktop integration (optional)

    ./install.sh              install for the current user
    ./install.sh --system     install under /usr/local (with sudo)
    ./install.sh --prefix DIR install under DIR
    ./install.sh --uninstall  remove it again

The desktop entry launches the headless runner in a terminal and is installed
into $XDG_DATA_HOME/applications (or /usr/local/share/applications). The game
directory is never copied; pass --game or set RA2_GAME_DIR. The default
$XDG_DATA_HOME/ra2-open-robot-arena/game location is checked automatically.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. Troubleshooting

  "no Robot Arena 2 installation found": the launcher lists every path it
  tried. Pass --game with the directory that directly contains RA2.cfz, UI/
  and Scripts/ (not its parent).

  "libpython3.12.so.1.0: missing": install the CPython 3.12 runtime; see
  section 3. `ldd bin/ra2-shell | grep libpython` shows the resolution.

  "Unable to find a GPU" / wgpu adapter error: install a Vulkan driver
  (mesa-vulkan-drivers) or set the software fallback your Mesa provides. The
  renderers are offscreen but still need an adapter.

  Missing textures or screens: check that the game directory is the complete
  install, not only the UI directory.

